# origin/main behaviour (baseline per maintainer decision 6)
# Generated by TestLegacyMenuLogs (pkg/characterization); regenerate with -update. Do not edit.
# Operation: logging.PrintLogs, -p/--print-logs, a log with lines (pkg/logging), run in a child process, stdout a pipe
# logFile: /tmp-root/var/log/hardn.log; hardn writes /tmp-root/var/log/hardn.log (/tmp-root stands for /)
# $PAGER: less, on PATH, a stand-in that records being run; not run.
# KNOWN-DEFECT: The whole file is printed at once, no pager, no tail and no count (file_logs_repository.go:89-96; logging.go:139-146): only the end stays on a terminal's screen, and what scrolled off is whatever the terminal keeps.
# NOTE: This golden holds logging.PrintLogs alone, not all of -p. On the root command's path (read, not run) stdout first gets the config line, "[INFO] Using configuration from: <path>" or the no-config lines (config.go:246, :252, :279), then the clear sequence and the ~~~ line even in a pipe (osdetect.go:50; utils.go:24-37), then "[SUCCESS] <os> detected" (osdetect.go:93-95), and those LogInfo and LogSuccess lines are also appended to the log on each -p (logging.go:99-100).
# NOTE: The "run <n>:" lines are the trunk's (next/v0.4), not origin/main's: pkg/host/runlog.go came with 6a04b467, LogFileOnly and revertFileLog with e264b8bb (next/p3-confirm-cleanup), none of them on origin/main. What prints them is origin/main's, on whatever the file holds.
# NOTE: -p is on the root command's Run, after the root check, the config load and DetectOS (cmd/hardn/main.go:148-152, :155, :184-188; read): a file of mode 0644 hardn refuses to print to another user, and a missing hardn.yml gets its offer first. TestDryRunAloneIsNotRefused holds -n -p reaching the root check.
# NOTE: Println adds a blank line to the file's last newline (file_logs_repository.go:96; logging.go:146).
# NOTE: A second copy of this function, pkg/utils.PrintLogs (utils.go:117), and a third in FileLogsRepository.PrintLogs (file_logs_repository.go:81), which the screen uses; see logs_parser.golden for the callers.
# The screen as printed, ESC as the four characters \x1b, each line ending in $; <no-newline> marks text with no final newline.
# ----
$
# Contents of /tmp-root/var/log/hardn.log:$
$
2026/10/29 08:12:44 INFO: Configuring DNS$
2026/10/29 08:12:44 INFO: run 1: $ resolvectl status$
2026/10/29 08:12:44 INFO: run 1: | Global$
2026/10/29 08:12:44 INFO: run 1: exit 0$
2026/10/29 08:12:45 ERROR: Failed to restart systemd-resolved$
$
